WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.008
[opening theme music playing]

01:04.189 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:06.066 --> 01:07.233
[car horn honks]

01:07.317 --> 01:09.319
[traffic noise]

01:09.819 --> 01:11.821
[kettle whistling]

01:13.073 --> 01:15.075
[liquid pouring]

01:20.455 --> 01:21.539
Are you even in charge here?

01:21.623 --> 01:22.832
Are you the presiding judge?

01:22.916 --> 01:26.461
Are you who decides what happens to us,
or do you answer to someone else?

01:26.544 --> 01:29.297
If you say I'm a thief, I'm a thief.
You say I go to jail, I go to jail?

01:29.380 --> 01:32.175
-Am I right?
-The ring next to the porcelain jar.

01:32.258 --> 01:34.260
-The diamond ring.
-[groans]

01:34.344 --> 01:37.013
No, look, I never saw a diamond ring.

01:37.889 --> 01:38.890
She doesn't have it.

01:39.766 --> 01:42.477
Who was that female officer?
Was it Yeon-sun?

01:42.560 --> 01:44.687
Tell her to come here. We need a pat down.

01:44.771 --> 01:45.855
[officer 2] Yes, sir.

01:46.648 --> 01:49.484
Why would anyone need to pat me down
if I am not a thief?

01:49.567 --> 01:51.820
Listen to her?
You're hiding something, aren't you?

01:52.403 --> 01:55.990
The lady turned a blind eye,
knowing this girl took money from the jar.

01:56.074 --> 01:58.868
-No, see, I earned that money, really.
-How did you earn it?

01:59.744 --> 02:00.787
Are you a tutor?

02:02.664 --> 02:04.666
[officer 2] She said
she cut this girl some slack

02:04.749 --> 02:07.752
and let her take the money
because she's a poor college student.

02:07.836 --> 02:09.087
[Geum-myeong groans]

02:09.170 --> 02:10.964
Not every poor person steals.

02:11.589 --> 02:13.925
You couldn't even beat
certain people into stealing.

02:14.008 --> 02:15.593
Let us pat you down, then.

02:16.177 --> 02:17.637
Oh, come on!

02:17.720 --> 02:20.640
Wait. I'm not a thief. Why must I undergo…

02:20.723 --> 02:22.016
I think you're shady.

02:22.100 --> 02:25.145
What's your home number?
I need to speak to your father.

02:25.228 --> 02:27.021
Oh, why would you need
to talk to my father

02:27.105 --> 02:28.857
if I'm not… I'm not a thief. Why?

02:28.940 --> 02:30.733
[officer 1] If you're innocent,
then call him.

02:30.817 --> 02:32.735
You're guilty.
That's why you're acting like this.

02:32.819 --> 02:35.947
If I told Dad I was suspected
of stealing something, he'd…

02:36.030 --> 02:38.158
he'd just be totally devastated!

02:38.241 --> 02:40.869
[car horn honking]

02:52.338 --> 02:53.923
This is the stop for everyone who lives--

02:54.007 --> 02:55.258
I get it. Go away.

02:55.925 --> 02:57.468
I'm waiting for the bus to take me home.

02:57.552 --> 02:58.595
And not to the base?

02:59.304 --> 03:02.265
-I, uh… I'm on leave until Friday.
-So go back early.

03:02.348 --> 03:03.391
Sorry?

03:03.474 --> 03:05.852
Geum-myeong is off-limits for you,
understand?

03:08.605 --> 03:09.689
Well? Answer me?

03:16.529 --> 03:17.572
You two…

03:19.657 --> 03:20.742
are dating?

03:22.368 --> 03:23.536
Are you trying to win me over?

03:26.289 --> 03:27.248
She dumped me.

03:27.332 --> 03:29.000
Dumped? You?

03:29.083 --> 03:30.543
I get dumped usually, sir.

03:31.836 --> 03:33.087
[laughs]

03:33.171 --> 03:34.005
Jeez.

03:34.756 --> 03:37.175
You spend all your time
chasing girls instead of studying.

03:37.258 --> 03:39.177
Well, of course
they break up with you, kid.

03:39.260 --> 03:43.056
Did your father really tell you to date
as many girls as you can in college?

03:43.681 --> 03:44.807
[Yeong-beom] Actually, sir,

03:45.934 --> 03:48.645
Geum-myeong's the only one.
She's dumped me eight times now.

03:55.276 --> 03:57.362
Would you like one?

03:57.445 --> 03:59.280
Oh, I'm fine. Keep it, Father.

03:59.781 --> 04:00.615
Oh!

04:03.159 --> 04:04.202
Uh, Mr. Yang.

04:05.453 --> 04:06.579
Have a safe trip back.

04:07.497 --> 04:08.331
So why?

04:10.124 --> 04:11.251
Why doesn't she like you?

04:13.461 --> 04:14.420
[chuckles]

04:16.172 --> 04:19.050
-I just think that--
-It's because you're too, just too…

04:19.133 --> 04:21.886
Boy, stay away, or I… I'll kill you!

04:22.804 --> 04:25.223
-It's not that.
-See, she had me for a father.

04:25.306 --> 04:27.475
Her standards are high.
Until she was five,

04:27.558 --> 04:29.560
she said she'd marry me
when she gets older.

04:29.644 --> 04:31.604
Clearly, you're not
good enough for her, all right?

04:31.688 --> 04:33.022
Just move on with your life now.

04:33.106 --> 04:34.941
It seems like
you're just not right for her.

04:35.441 --> 04:37.568
But the reason
we're off and on a lot, sir--

04:37.652 --> 04:38.820
Off and on so much?

04:39.904 --> 04:41.281
-Uh…
-What?

04:44.033 --> 04:47.161
She always says, "Cat got your tongue?
Why aren't you saying anything?"

04:47.245 --> 04:49.247
[gong sounds]

04:50.331 --> 04:53.418
Cat got your tongue or what?
Why aren't you saying anything?

04:53.501 --> 04:54.419
[Ae-sun] So I'm ready.

04:54.502 --> 04:56.671
[Gwan-sik] Take this ring,
and it's a done deal.

04:56.754 --> 04:57.922
"When," I said.

05:01.050 --> 05:03.678
[car horn honking]

05:04.679 --> 05:07.140
-Um, um… So…
-[jaunty music playing]

05:08.057 --> 05:09.642
Since you did offer it…

05:09.726 --> 05:11.019
[Yeong-beom straining]

05:13.813 --> 05:15.231
[middle-aged Gwan-sik] No.

05:17.442 --> 05:18.318
Go away.

05:23.156 --> 05:24.657
[gong sounds]

05:33.082 --> 05:34.375
You lied about the ring?

05:37.128 --> 05:38.338
She didn't take it, right?

05:44.594 --> 05:46.012
[housekeeper] Goodness gracious.

05:46.554 --> 05:48.556
[Jenny] Why did you need
to send her to the police?

05:48.639 --> 05:50.433
Typically, you just frame and fire them.

05:52.101 --> 05:54.062
[Jenny's mom]
Nobody would believe a thief.

05:54.145 --> 05:55.980
We make her look like a thief

05:56.064 --> 05:58.608
so she starts saying all kinds of things.

05:58.691 --> 06:00.902
That way, it won't backfire on us.

06:01.486 --> 06:03.696
What if she starts a rumor
about Oh Jenny from Daechi-dong

06:03.780 --> 06:06.366
who's looking for someone
to take the test in her place?

06:06.449 --> 06:08.618
Then we need to cope with all that shit.

06:08.701 --> 06:11.621
So that girl stole the ring,
and she's the thief.

06:17.960 --> 06:19.629
Don't I always tell you?

06:19.712 --> 06:22.757
In life, you either
have the upper hand, or you don't.

06:23.341 --> 06:25.760
You're either the hunter or the hunted.

06:26.803 --> 06:28.096
It's decided in a moment.

06:29.097 --> 06:32.517
There's absolutely no need
to pity the losers.

06:33.351 --> 06:35.144
Don't waste time
with crap like compassion.

06:35.228 --> 06:38.439
You've got to be ruthless with folks.
That's how I made my money.

06:40.900 --> 06:42.443
[Jenny] So you keep making good money.

06:42.944 --> 06:44.695
If you lose your spunk, we're done.

06:45.738 --> 06:46.572
What?

06:47.365 --> 06:48.324
I'm learning from you.

06:51.119 --> 06:54.080
You're saying she stole
the flower-shaped ring

06:54.163 --> 06:55.873
that's always been here.

06:56.833 --> 06:58.626
Is that what you're trying to say?

06:59.210 --> 07:00.128
Huh? Yeah.

07:01.129 --> 07:02.422
How dare she.

07:03.840 --> 07:06.801
-It's a diamond ring.
-Yes. Diamond.

07:07.552 --> 07:09.429
[housekeeper] How many carats was it?

07:10.054 --> 07:11.389
About half a carat?

07:12.515 --> 07:14.058
How much was it?

07:14.600 --> 07:15.476
It's pricey.

07:16.352 --> 07:17.937
[housekeeper] Flower-shaped?

07:18.020 --> 07:21.524
Yes, flower-shaped. Quit it, lady!
You even know what you're saying, huh?

07:21.607 --> 07:23.985
Oh my. Look, here it is.

07:24.569 --> 07:25.945
I found it.

07:26.946 --> 07:27.905
It's right here.

07:29.782 --> 07:32.577
Oh, it must've fallen on its own.

07:33.744 --> 07:35.204
[jaunty music playing]

07:36.414 --> 07:39.125
You should
call the authorities now, right?

07:39.208 --> 07:40.501
Lady, what are you doing?

07:40.585 --> 07:43.379
Call the police.
Make sure they know it's here.

07:44.255 --> 07:47.633
-Say sorry about the confusion.
-What the hell are you trying to do?

07:49.343 --> 07:50.928
So you won't call, then?

07:53.848 --> 07:55.475
Are you deaf or what?

07:58.269 --> 07:59.729
[distant siren wailing]

07:59.812 --> 08:01.689
If you don't, I will throw it out.

08:03.232 --> 08:04.525
Are you out of your head?

08:04.609 --> 08:06.986
Do you have any idea how expensive it is?

08:07.069 --> 08:09.530
-Damn it, woman!
-But you already lost it, right?

08:10.156 --> 08:13.284
Yes, you reported it stolen
and said the girl was the thief?

08:13.367 --> 08:16.412
Are you gonna tell the cops
that I threw it down to the street?

08:17.497 --> 08:20.124
[screams] How dare you! You better not!

08:20.208 --> 08:24.837
You know me.
I'd throw this very far. Look.

08:24.921 --> 08:26.714
[screams]

08:28.799 --> 08:31.594
[grunts] That ring's worth more
than you are!

08:32.345 --> 08:33.179
Call them.

08:34.430 --> 08:37.517
You bitch. You better stay out of
my goddamn business.

08:38.017 --> 08:39.435
Apologize.

08:39.519 --> 08:42.271
Who do you think you are?
Mind your business. Do you know her?

08:43.564 --> 08:45.107
-I do.
-God!

08:45.191 --> 08:47.068
I'm gonna lose my mind, damn it!

08:47.151 --> 08:48.236
Call them right now!

08:49.487 --> 08:51.489
[jaunty music continues]

08:53.533 --> 08:54.951
[phone ringing]

08:56.327 --> 08:57.745
[phone ringing]

09:00.623 --> 09:01.457
Hello?

09:02.875 --> 09:04.210
What now? You need cash?

09:04.710 --> 09:05.628
We don't have any.

09:08.297 --> 09:09.298
Geum-myeong's mom!

09:09.799 --> 09:11.092
Your baby's calling.

09:11.175 --> 09:13.052
Oh! My baby!

09:13.803 --> 09:15.596
-Oh dear!
-Baby? Seriously?

09:16.722 --> 09:18.975
Hi, dear. Where are you? Where?

09:19.058 --> 09:20.518
She's out spending your money again.

09:21.686 --> 09:23.521
[Geum-myeong] I wanted to cry like a baby

09:23.604 --> 09:26.274
and tell her that people in Seoul
were really evil.

09:26.357 --> 09:28.484
[middle-aged Ae-sun] Baby, have you eaten?

09:29.068 --> 09:33.072
[Geum-myeong] But I just couldn't speak…
when I heard her voice.

09:33.155 --> 09:35.032
Yes, of course I have eaten, Mom.

09:35.533 --> 09:37.368
[Geum-myeong] The anger in me melted away.

09:37.451 --> 09:40.079
No, no reason. I just wanted to call.

09:41.247 --> 09:43.499
Can't I call just because I feel like it?

09:44.542 --> 09:46.127
[sighs] I do.

09:48.546 --> 09:49.714
I have cash.

09:52.341 --> 09:53.384
What about you?

09:54.343 --> 09:55.386
Everything good?

09:57.763 --> 09:58.848
[groans]

09:58.931 --> 10:01.726
Come on, Mom.
I told you to stop street vending.

10:01.809 --> 10:05.062
I hate how you have to eat
sitting out on the street there every day.

10:05.563 --> 10:06.856
[groans]

10:06.939 --> 10:08.190
Those damned abalones.

10:09.066 --> 10:10.484
Abalones. Oh God.

10:11.027 --> 10:12.778
What is the damn deal with abalone?

10:12.862 --> 10:15.531
Your back always hurts.
Set up a store or something.

10:15.615 --> 10:18.159
We don't have enough to start a store.

10:18.242 --> 10:19.994
[sighs] Mom.

10:22.705 --> 10:24.540
Why don't you ever have any money?

10:25.082 --> 10:27.001
[middle-aged Ae-sun laughs]

10:27.835 --> 10:29.045
I know, right?

10:29.128 --> 10:31.631
Oh, why don't I ever have money, huh?

10:31.714 --> 10:34.550
-Because of you! Because of you!
-[whispers] Quiet.

10:35.134 --> 10:37.553
[Geum-myeong] I was mad at my mom
for being poor.

10:38.262 --> 10:40.723
I knew she was poor because of me.

10:40.806 --> 10:42.767
[wistful music playing]

10:42.850 --> 10:45.186
Baby, you haven't seen Dad yet.

10:45.269 --> 10:47.355
Did you call me because you saw him?

10:47.438 --> 10:48.314
Dad's coming?

10:48.397 --> 10:51.233
Your father got a reward
for saving that man from drowning.

10:51.317 --> 10:53.319
I told you he was going to the mainland.

10:53.402 --> 10:57.823
The governor sent him and a few villagers
over there for vacation.

10:58.366 --> 11:02.787
He gave them museum tickets
because a… a new one opened or something.

11:02.870 --> 11:05.122
Where on the mainland? Which museum is it?

11:05.206 --> 11:07.958
He wanted to see you
if you could make time for it.

11:08.042 --> 11:09.377
Uh, where on the mainland?

11:09.460 --> 11:12.171
On the mainland.

11:12.254 --> 11:14.131
The one museum that opened, you know.

11:14.215 --> 11:17.760
God, if you just say "the mainland,"
how am I supposed to know where that is?

11:17.843 --> 11:20.137
And the museum, where is it?

11:20.680 --> 11:23.307
I'm busy, Mom. What do you want me to do
if you visit without notice?

11:23.933 --> 11:26.519
So tell me,
is Dad coming to see me or not?

11:27.687 --> 11:30.356
Geum-myeong, he'll get there.

11:30.856 --> 11:32.358
Dad will go see you.

11:33.275 --> 11:36.112
[chanting] …for Kim Yeong-sam!

11:36.195 --> 11:39.699
We will vote for Kim Yeong-sam!
We will vote for Kim Yeong-sam!

11:44.453 --> 11:46.747
[Geum-myeong] My God,
the traffic is terrible.

11:47.915 --> 11:49.875
[girl 1] She's basically mentally ill.

11:50.376 --> 11:52.586
How can she accuse you of being a thief?

11:53.421 --> 11:55.047
Did the cops call your house?

11:55.131 --> 11:56.382
Oh, no.

11:57.800 --> 11:59.802
I didn't give them my home number.

12:03.514 --> 12:04.557
[buzzer sounds]

12:05.182 --> 12:06.851
You're not going to tell your family?

12:06.934 --> 12:08.269
No way. I can't.

12:12.314 --> 12:14.233
I don't care if everyone knows.

12:15.276 --> 12:17.153
As long as my parents don't find out.

12:21.115 --> 12:24.869
[Geum-myeong] Parents never have
any idea of the instant

12:24.952 --> 12:27.121
when their child's heart gets wounded.

12:28.330 --> 12:31.208
If they do notice,
they will try to protect their child.

12:35.129 --> 12:37.548
So God prevents them from finding out.

12:40.259 --> 12:42.219
[tender music playing]

12:42.303 --> 12:44.722
No child can grow up without heartbreak.

12:44.805 --> 12:47.016
But God knows a father's heart

12:47.099 --> 12:49.643
will break if he finds out
his child is wounded,

12:49.727 --> 12:52.688
so God makes the child
keep quiet about her wounds.

12:58.861 --> 12:59.862
Goodness.

12:59.945 --> 13:02.990
You'll be the absolute death of me.
My God, Dad.

13:03.574 --> 13:05.242
I could've been really late!

13:05.326 --> 13:07.411
It's cold out. It's colder at night.

13:08.162 --> 13:10.122
How long have you been waiting, Dad?

13:10.206 --> 13:12.124
Do all college kids have these books?

13:12.208 --> 13:14.168
[Geum-myeong] What time did you get here?

13:16.629 --> 13:18.547
Let's go. Go. [chuckles]

13:20.174 --> 13:23.594
Isn't this bothering you all the time?
Why is your strap always twisted?

13:26.514 --> 13:28.516
[tender music continues]

13:40.528 --> 13:41.779
[Geum-myeong sighs]

13:41.862 --> 13:43.656
[music fades]

13:48.994 --> 13:50.120
[Geum-myeong sighs]

13:51.956 --> 13:54.083
So did you come to Seoul to eat jjamppong?

13:55.251 --> 13:56.544
Aren't we going to talk?

13:59.213 --> 14:00.172
You drink too.

14:01.841 --> 14:03.050
I hold my liquor.

14:10.266 --> 14:12.893
So you don't go to
student protests, do you?

14:12.977 --> 14:14.895
There isn't a new museum, is there?

14:15.813 --> 14:17.189
Where are you staying?

14:17.273 --> 14:18.566
I just stopped to look.

14:19.149 --> 14:21.527
Tear gas is very painful.
The tears don't stop.

14:22.027 --> 14:23.362
Which subway line is it?

14:24.071 --> 14:24.947
Can you go alone?

14:25.698 --> 14:26.657
You're not dating

14:27.741 --> 14:29.827
some soldier, are you, honey?

14:30.494 --> 14:32.538
-You shouldn't date them.
-[sighs]

14:32.621 --> 14:35.040
Why are we having dinner
if this is how it'll go?

14:35.749 --> 14:37.501
We're talking of different things.

14:45.718 --> 14:47.261
I quit my part-time job.

14:48.512 --> 14:50.306
I got kicked out of residence.

14:51.181 --> 14:52.933
My scholarship's running out.

14:56.854 --> 14:57.771
That's okay.

15:02.776 --> 15:05.279
All these kids
were top students in high school.

15:05.362 --> 15:08.741
Basically, your school's all big fish
that came out of a small pond.

15:09.241 --> 15:11.869
You can't always be the top student.
It's impossible.

15:12.578 --> 15:16.123
I never ate lunch with kids
like that at school.

15:18.167 --> 15:19.209
[sighs]

15:21.670 --> 15:23.547
"A big fish from a small pond."

15:24.882 --> 15:26.550
I really hate that saying.

15:29.803 --> 15:33.307
What good is it that you're a fish
that made it out of the pond?

15:34.558 --> 15:36.435
What if you're from a small pond?

15:37.937 --> 15:40.064
So what if you were the best there?

15:43.442 --> 15:45.277
I got into the study abroad program.

15:47.404 --> 15:48.489
But I won't go.

15:51.867 --> 15:54.328
I really, really hate that Oh Ye-rim

15:54.828 --> 15:56.664
is going to go instead, but…

15:58.749 --> 15:59.917
but I won't go.

16:07.883 --> 16:09.802
I want to study abroad.

16:10.302 --> 16:12.930
I… I don't wanna be
at that damn part-time job.

16:13.013 --> 16:15.140
I wanna be doing tons of things.

16:16.558 --> 16:17.893
And I won't get to.

16:20.729 --> 16:23.065
I'm just very greedy, I suppose.

16:24.942 --> 16:26.902
I'm being egotistical.

16:29.446 --> 16:30.406
[Geum-myeong sighs]

16:30.990 --> 16:33.033
I want to soar high above it all.

16:37.204 --> 16:39.206
There's always something holding me back.

16:40.833 --> 16:42.084
Is it Mom and Dad?

16:42.668 --> 16:43.627
Oh, no.

16:46.005 --> 16:47.506
My guilt. Mine.

16:48.716 --> 16:50.676
The higher I want to soar…

16:50.759 --> 16:52.761
[tender piano music playing]

16:53.679 --> 16:55.806
…the stronger my guilt holds me back.

16:57.057 --> 17:00.436
Why should I feel bad that I want
to do more than others, Dad?

17:02.521 --> 17:03.605
[sighs]

17:03.689 --> 17:05.524
It's all so infuriating.

17:07.818 --> 17:10.446
[Geum-myeong] I just wanted
to say I was sorry,

17:11.030 --> 17:15.451
but everything that I spewed at Dad
turned into thorns.

17:18.829 --> 17:19.663
Geum-myeong.

17:20.998 --> 17:21.832
What, Dad?

17:23.709 --> 17:24.543
Do it.

17:25.878 --> 17:26.795
Do it all.

17:29.131 --> 17:31.091
I'm still here for you, dear.

17:43.979 --> 17:44.938
[Gwan-sik] Geum-myeong,

17:45.773 --> 17:46.857
tell your teacher

17:48.692 --> 17:51.195
I'll pay your school fees
in three days, okay?

17:54.782 --> 17:56.825
[middle-aged Gwan-sik chuckles]

17:56.909 --> 17:58.327
I'm still here for you.

18:05.918 --> 18:07.628
I'm no longer a child.

18:07.711 --> 18:09.838
Why do you still keep
giving me your squid?

18:11.632 --> 18:13.342
[music fades]

18:17.137 --> 18:19.014
[middle-aged Gwan-sik]
I want you to find a place

18:19.098 --> 18:20.724
in a safe neighborhood.

18:21.308 --> 18:22.392
Don't worry about rent.

18:23.018 --> 18:25.395
The sea has fish, um, you see.

18:25.479 --> 18:28.357
All I really have to do
is catch them all first, dear.

18:31.026 --> 18:32.694
And don't date military guys.

18:33.529 --> 18:34.863
Don't abuse hard liquor.

18:35.572 --> 18:37.116
Don't go to student protests.

18:37.199 --> 18:40.452
Tear gas is very painful.
You can't stop crying.

18:46.542 --> 18:48.627
The stuff on the news scares me the most.

18:49.461 --> 18:50.587
I don't know anything.

18:51.296 --> 18:52.464
I really don't.

18:53.382 --> 18:54.383
Sleeping is hard

18:54.466 --> 18:58.512
when I see soldiers
with batons in their hands on the news.

18:59.012 --> 19:02.015
Just hearing that young college kids
get beaten up at protests…

19:03.767 --> 19:04.852
Oh God, I'm…

19:07.396 --> 19:09.439
It makes me shiver in fear.

19:11.567 --> 19:12.693
So, Geum-myeong,

19:13.735 --> 19:14.820
if possible…

19:18.198 --> 19:20.576
[indistinct chattering]

19:20.659 --> 19:21.535
[man] Be quiet!

19:22.327 --> 19:23.537
I'm trying to hear this.

19:24.538 --> 19:26.707
-I said be quiet!
-Oh, it's so annoying.

19:27.374 --> 19:28.208
What?

19:28.834 --> 19:31.044
Oh, but did you vote for someone else?

19:31.128 --> 19:33.714
[Geum-myeong sobs] You're frustrating.

19:36.133 --> 19:37.968
You're frustrating, Dad.

19:42.264 --> 19:45.434
You said you came to see me
because the museum was nearby.

19:45.517 --> 19:47.394
This is so far away from here!

19:49.354 --> 19:50.606
[crying]

19:52.816 --> 19:54.109
[woman] Please tone it down!

19:55.152 --> 19:56.570
[Geum-myeong sobs]

19:56.653 --> 19:58.030
It's very hard for you to visit.

19:59.072 --> 20:00.324
We're far away too.

20:00.949 --> 20:03.577
-[wistful piano music playing]
-[sniffles]

20:07.372 --> 20:09.750
[crying]

20:11.501 --> 20:14.004
[middle-aged Ae-sun]
Geum-myeong, he'll get there.

20:14.713 --> 20:16.173
Dad will go see you.

20:16.924 --> 20:20.469
He never goes on a vacation.
You know that.

20:21.220 --> 20:24.514
Even if it's New Year's or Chuseok,

20:25.057 --> 20:26.642
he goes fishing.

20:26.725 --> 20:29.186
He just took this chance to see you.

20:30.020 --> 20:31.063
But I have my own

20:32.314 --> 20:33.649
stuff going on too.

20:33.732 --> 20:38.153
Baby, he would really like
to visit his eldest daughter.

20:38.862 --> 20:41.365
So listen up, Geum-myeong,
if you see your dad…

20:41.448 --> 20:44.117
YONGSAN INTERCITY BUS STATION

20:59.967 --> 21:01.009
[sighs]

21:05.639 --> 21:08.517
Cheonan to Seoul.
Why would he come all this way?

21:09.893 --> 21:10.769
So annoying.

21:12.396 --> 21:14.189
[middle-aged Ae-sun]
So listen up, Geum-myeong,

21:14.273 --> 21:17.234
if you see your dad,
don't lose your temper.

21:17.317 --> 21:19.236
Be sweet to your father, okay?

21:19.319 --> 21:22.322
His affection for you has been
one-sided for 20 years.

21:28.412 --> 21:30.706
[melodic pop music playing]

21:40.674 --> 21:42.301
[Ae-sun] Catch a lot of fish!

21:42.384 --> 21:44.469
Catch so many squids for me!

21:54.229 --> 21:55.814
[melodic pop music continues]

22:13.498 --> 22:16.335
Oh no, I'm leaving
that little thing on her own.

22:18.503 --> 22:21.256
[Geum-myeong] Dad felt bad
about leaving behind a daughter who,

22:21.340 --> 22:22.424
in his eyes,

22:22.966 --> 22:24.217
would never grow up.

22:27.846 --> 22:31.433
Because I'll always be
a young girl to him.

22:33.685 --> 22:36.146
FROM YANG EUN-MYEONG (CLASS 2-7)

22:36.730 --> 22:38.857
What am I gonna say? What am I gonna say?

22:39.691 --> 22:41.401
I'm not good at things like this.

22:43.862 --> 22:46.656
Tell the kids who bought those plastic
"S" letters to give them back.

22:46.740 --> 22:49.409
Just return their cash
and take back the letters, understand?

22:49.493 --> 22:51.787
They keep saying they don't
have them anymore though.

22:51.870 --> 22:53.580
Do you know what this scotch cost, huh?

22:53.663 --> 22:55.791
Or how much I work to make this much?

22:57.793 --> 22:58.919
[Geum-myeong] That fall…

22:59.002 --> 23:01.421
Oh, harvesting season of my life, my foot.

23:02.214 --> 23:04.424
The older you get,
the more you take from me.

23:06.009 --> 23:07.677
You took the harvest of my life.

23:12.265 --> 23:14.226
Home room is Sonata.
Your principal is Stellar.

23:14.309 --> 23:15.727
Chinese Writing is Pony, right?

23:15.811 --> 23:16.770
-Uh, yeah.
-Huh?

23:18.271 --> 23:21.108
Oh, hello, sir. Hello, sir.

23:22.484 --> 23:24.569
[chuckles] Hello there.

23:25.779 --> 23:27.531
[Geum-myeong]
Everything she reaped and sowed

23:27.614 --> 23:29.199
was taken away back then.

23:29.282 --> 23:31.284
[footsteps approaching]

23:35.664 --> 23:37.332
[Jenny's mom] Is that your booze?

23:38.125 --> 23:40.836
So how do you know that girl anyway?

23:41.461 --> 23:43.171
Is she your daughter or something?

23:45.048 --> 23:46.049
I know her.

23:46.550 --> 23:48.051
Yes, yes, sure you do.

23:49.928 --> 23:52.431
-[Ae-sun] I've had enough freebies.
-[Gwan-sik] Those free things?

23:52.514 --> 23:54.891
Listen up.
If you get drunk, they will rob you.

23:54.975 --> 23:57.519
She said to drink it all
and melt like butter, right?

23:57.602 --> 23:58.728
Who are you guys?

23:58.812 --> 24:00.939
Be careful.
Just don't turn off the lights, okay?

24:01.022 --> 24:02.858
That woman is an actual thief.

24:02.941 --> 24:04.985
She will steal your suitcase
when you sleep.

24:06.653 --> 24:07.988
Yeah, but why tell me this?

24:08.989 --> 24:11.324
-Huh?
-Why are you telling me this?

24:21.001 --> 24:22.294
So why did you help me?

24:23.211 --> 24:24.379
Why did you bother at all?

24:25.297 --> 24:26.298
Aren't I a stranger?

24:26.965 --> 24:28.008
What am I to you?

24:29.593 --> 24:30.427
Why?

24:31.428 --> 24:32.262
Why?

24:34.598 --> 24:35.515
It'd be terrible.

24:36.099 --> 24:38.894
It'd be terrible
if your suitcase was stolen too.

24:41.146 --> 24:42.022
That's all it is?

24:43.273 --> 24:45.692
We didn't want something awful
to happen to you.

24:53.158 --> 24:54.451
[young housekeeper] You're right.

24:55.243 --> 24:57.871
We don't want bad things for each other.

25:08.798 --> 25:11.343
No, we don't want bad things
for each other.

25:11.927 --> 25:15.180
I'd be so upset if that child
was wrongfully accused of stealing.

25:15.263 --> 25:18.475
Wow, might as well be
Mother Teresa talking like that.

25:19.059 --> 25:21.770
You don't know that girl
or Seoul National University.

25:23.855 --> 25:25.815
And you're always so nosy about things.

25:25.899 --> 25:27.067
[laughs]

25:27.567 --> 25:28.485
I do.

25:29.027 --> 25:31.780
She guarded my mom's inheritance
when I was a kid.

25:31.863 --> 25:34.449
Lady, that girl
was not even alive at the time.

25:35.033 --> 25:36.326
Similar looks.

25:36.409 --> 25:37.827
My goodness.

25:37.911 --> 25:40.622
If you weren't connected with that
boss lady, I'd have seen to it…

25:40.705 --> 25:42.374
What? [chuckles]

25:42.457 --> 25:44.459
You'd make me a thief
and get me canned too?

25:48.964 --> 25:49.923
Miss Kim.

25:50.674 --> 25:52.050
It's ma'am to you.

25:54.886 --> 25:55.720
Miss Kim.

25:55.804 --> 25:58.431
Quit calling me "Miss Kim"
in front of my daughter.

25:58.932 --> 26:02.269
Why do you live such a terrible life
when you adore your daughter?

26:03.103 --> 26:05.772
You know she watches every move you make.

26:06.773 --> 26:09.442
Shit! I told you to
throw out the ones that are dead.

26:09.526 --> 26:11.778
-[lighter clatters]
-Be good to each other.

26:12.320 --> 26:13.655
-Just be good.
-[sighs]

26:13.738 --> 26:15.574
Parents' virtue and goodness

26:16.449 --> 26:17.909
are passed on to their children.

26:18.827 --> 26:19.661
Look.

26:20.787 --> 26:21.830
I'm serious.

26:22.414 --> 26:23.915
You can tell she's on a bad road.

26:24.583 --> 26:26.167
I know already.

26:30.630 --> 26:32.465
[both sigh]

26:33.341 --> 26:35.719
-[camera shutter clicks]
-[upbeat music playing]

26:38.430 --> 26:39.889
[Jenny] My mom made me do it.

26:40.390 --> 26:41.766
[train horn blares]

26:41.850 --> 26:45.395
SEOUL STATION

26:46.396 --> 26:47.522
[sighs]

26:50.150 --> 26:52.569
[sobs, sniffles]

26:53.236 --> 26:54.821
[sobs]

26:55.405 --> 26:57.157
[sobs, sniffles]

26:57.741 --> 26:59.784
How can I leave if
you're standing there like that?

26:59.868 --> 27:02.287
Then stay with me. Don't go.

27:02.370 --> 27:05.373
[both crying]

27:05.457 --> 27:07.584
So, are we together again then, honey?

27:08.418 --> 27:11.087
I don't know. Just stay still.

27:11.171 --> 27:14.841
Please stop upsetting me.
I might become a deserter at this rate.

27:14.924 --> 27:17.594
But… but how long will you serve?

27:18.720 --> 27:20.597
797 days.

27:20.680 --> 27:22.682
[crying]

27:23.391 --> 27:26.227
Oh God, I hate the DPRK.

27:26.311 --> 27:28.855
We can continue this on-and-off romance.

27:29.481 --> 27:31.733
But if you get married,
choose me, will you?

27:32.692 --> 27:33.652
We'll see.

27:34.277 --> 27:37.739
-We'll see how good you are to me.
-You said you'd marry me last time.

27:37.822 --> 27:40.325
So? How do I know if that's right?

27:40.950 --> 27:43.912
They say you don't know
up until you walk down the aisle.

27:45.121 --> 27:46.873
[Yeong-beom] Just watch, okay?

27:46.956 --> 27:48.875
I'm gonna see you in a wedding dress.

27:48.958 --> 27:51.670
[Geum-myeong] No matter how much
I believed I was different from Mom…

27:51.753 --> 27:53.421
Hey, you boarding the train or what?

27:53.922 --> 27:56.800
…I was exactly like her.

27:57.884 --> 27:59.469
But I also wasn't.

27:59.552 --> 28:01.554
[crying]

28:03.682 --> 28:05.850
[man] The bride will now enter
to walk down the aisle.

28:05.934 --> 28:07.352
[crying]

28:08.520 --> 28:09.854
-Geum-myeong.
-[sniffles]

28:10.897 --> 28:13.108
Daddy's right here next to you, okay?

28:13.608 --> 28:16.611
You do what you want, baby girl.
Just do whatever you please.

28:16.695 --> 28:18.446
[crying]

28:30.709 --> 28:33.378
[Geum-myeong] Mom's love story
was a fairy tale.

28:33.461 --> 28:35.630
[man] Please welcome the bride.

28:35.714 --> 28:37.799
["Bridal Chorus" playing on piano]

28:37.882 --> 28:40.176
[guests cheering, clapping]

28:40.260 --> 28:43.638
[Geum-myeong] Will my love story
also be one?

28:45.265 --> 28:46.933
'67 THE 7TH HALLA CHUNSA FESTIVAL

28:47.016 --> 28:49.811
-[festive music playing]
-[children laughing]

28:51.730 --> 28:53.106
Stop bumping into everyone.

29:00.697 --> 29:02.240
-[man] Here you are. Enjoy.
-Thank you.

29:02.323 --> 29:03.533
[man] Yes, sure, sure.

29:10.248 --> 29:12.041
THEME
JEJU, SPRING BREEZE, WIND

29:27.098 --> 29:28.099
[Geum-myeong] "Jeju."

29:28.600 --> 29:32.353
"Dodong Girls' High School,
sophomore, class five. Oh Ae-sun."

29:34.230 --> 29:36.107
Ten thousand waves

29:36.191 --> 29:37.650
Ten thousand winds

29:38.151 --> 29:39.486
A rock still remains

29:40.403 --> 29:42.280
A rock that never moves

29:42.822 --> 29:44.032
From my heart

29:46.576 --> 29:47.577
[Ae-sun sighs]

29:58.004 --> 29:58.963
My mom

30:05.386 --> 30:06.596
[groans]

30:07.180 --> 30:10.850
I begged you not to sit next to me.
You're not supposed to be on this side.

30:12.769 --> 30:14.521
You should be
at practice right now, Gwan-sik.

30:14.604 --> 30:15.897
What are you doing here?

30:16.564 --> 30:19.567
I raised my hand
and said I… wanted to see you.

30:20.819 --> 30:22.987
You know what people say around town?

30:23.071 --> 30:26.491
They say Gwan-sik wakes up
just so he can follow Ae-sun around.

30:26.991 --> 30:29.494
You will win this. 100%.

30:31.246 --> 30:33.665
I think you're going to be
a renowned poet, Ae-sun.

30:34.165 --> 30:35.208
A renowned poet.

30:37.627 --> 30:39.128
-Think so?
-Mm.

30:40.713 --> 30:42.173
Well, what do you know?

30:43.466 --> 30:44.300
Nothing really.

30:45.343 --> 30:46.177
I can't write.

30:56.729 --> 30:57.605
[sighs]

30:58.189 --> 31:00.191
I'll send an anonymous complaint
to the board.

31:00.984 --> 31:02.694
Athletes need to study hard too.

31:02.777 --> 31:05.196
It's not like
they're going to provide for your future.

31:05.697 --> 31:07.615
This is so upsetting, seriously.

31:09.576 --> 31:11.578
A moth? Erase it. Why did you draw a moth?

31:11.661 --> 31:12.704
Butterfly.

31:12.787 --> 31:13.955
Jeez.

31:14.873 --> 31:16.457
Can you write me a poem too?

31:17.083 --> 31:19.127
Name it "Yang Gwan-sik," dear.

31:19.210 --> 31:21.671
[feel-good music playing]

31:21.754 --> 31:22.589
Why would I?

31:33.516 --> 31:35.518
[feel-good music continues]

31:43.109 --> 31:44.736
[woman] Rice cake for sale!

31:44.819 --> 31:48.072
In life, you never know what will happen
unless you go for it.

31:49.032 --> 31:51.534
Who knew that I'd still be sitting here

31:52.452 --> 31:53.828
20 years later?

31:53.912 --> 31:57.582
THE 28TH HALLA CHUNSA WRITING CONTEST

31:57.665 --> 31:59.792
THEME
SPRING, WIND, MOON

32:01.002 --> 32:01.836
Submit this.

32:02.921 --> 32:04.255
FALL BREEZE
OH AE-SUN

32:04.339 --> 32:06.341
[middle-aged Ae-sun]
I'm not in high school anymore.

32:07.467 --> 32:11.095
The sheet was just lying on the ground,
so I just scribbled a few lines.

32:11.179 --> 32:13.348
I still think you better send it in.

32:13.431 --> 32:15.642
[chuckles] No, I'm not sure.

32:16.768 --> 32:19.896
Sports day tomorrow is canceled again.

32:19.979 --> 32:20.813
Why?

32:20.897 --> 32:23.691
Well, they're rehearsing for the Olympics.

32:23.775 --> 32:24.609
All the time.

32:24.692 --> 32:25.777
[groans]

32:26.569 --> 32:28.655
We get the most sales
on sports day though.

32:29.656 --> 32:31.240
What about starting a store?

32:31.324 --> 32:32.951
We might even take out a loan.

32:33.034 --> 32:36.746
I'm fed up of
carrying this bundle everywhere.

32:38.498 --> 32:39.916
[woman] Excuse me.

32:39.999 --> 32:42.210
Oh, hello. Would you like to try some?

32:42.794 --> 32:45.254
Ae-sun? You're Ae-sun, right?

32:45.338 --> 32:47.298
I'm Chang-suk. Go Chang-suk.

32:47.382 --> 32:48.967
We went to high school together.

32:50.385 --> 32:53.388
Oh, Ch… Chang-suk.

32:54.013 --> 32:57.183
How long has it been?
I haven't seen you since school, have I?

32:57.976 --> 32:59.936
All the girls are wondering
what you're up to.

33:00.019 --> 33:02.021
Why don't you come to reunions?

33:02.105 --> 33:03.690
Oh, do you not get them?

33:03.773 --> 33:05.191
The reunion invites?

33:05.274 --> 33:07.902
Is your info not on record
because you were expelled?

33:07.986 --> 33:09.237
[chuckles]

33:09.320 --> 33:11.906
Oh, I… Why don't I give you some for free?

33:11.990 --> 33:13.408
I'll… I'll give you plenty.

33:14.242 --> 33:15.785
-These are real.
-Oh God.

33:15.868 --> 33:18.037
The poor woman can't even look at him.

33:18.830 --> 33:21.499
Is she, uh, self-conscious about school?

33:21.582 --> 33:24.544
Oh no, not the old friend from school.

33:31.759 --> 33:34.178
[wistful music playing]

33:34.262 --> 33:37.682
[Geum-myeong] Mom could never look
at children his age.

33:44.355 --> 33:46.274
[middle-aged Gwan-sik sighs]
How old are you?

33:48.234 --> 33:49.360
[boy] Fifteen.

33:50.028 --> 33:51.404
Year of the Tiger.

33:56.868 --> 33:57.994
[boy 2] Hey, where?

33:59.829 --> 34:01.289
Is that "in" these days?

34:02.248 --> 34:04.584
-Sorry?
-What else is popular right now?

34:05.460 --> 34:06.711
Thank you, mister.

34:08.254 --> 34:10.465
Of course. Be sure to enjoy, kids.

34:10.548 --> 34:11.466
Yes, sir.

34:15.595 --> 34:17.096
[Geum-myeong] In Dad's heart,

34:17.597 --> 34:20.683
Dong-myeong kept growing up.

34:23.603 --> 34:26.522
I think that sympathy
truly is also a part of evolution.

34:27.106 --> 34:31.069
Look at the grandmothers in the country.
They go on fine after their kids die.

34:31.152 --> 34:33.571
They'd have eight kids, and two would die.

34:33.654 --> 34:36.240
They'd casually say things like,
"You had a brother once,"

34:36.324 --> 34:37.158
like it's nothing.

34:37.241 --> 34:38.868
-Mm.
-[Ye-rim] Does that make sense?

34:38.951 --> 34:40.745
How do you live after losing a child?

34:41.245 --> 34:42.205
But they do.

34:42.288 --> 34:45.249
What are they supposed to do?
Cry every day? Starve themselves?

34:45.833 --> 34:47.376
No, no, the point of this is

34:47.460 --> 34:50.880
to prove the correlation between
empathy and developing civilization.

34:51.464 --> 34:52.298
Right?

34:55.051 --> 34:56.803
[Geum-myeong]
Because you're better than them?

34:59.263 --> 35:00.098
What?

35:00.681 --> 35:03.434
You think they live that way
because they're less civilized?

35:04.185 --> 35:05.019
[sighs]

35:06.062 --> 35:08.314
[Ye-rim] Just keep on dusting away
your eraser debris.

35:09.357 --> 35:11.484
It's not because
they're not as good-natured as you.

35:12.068 --> 35:13.194
They pretend nothing's wrong

35:13.277 --> 35:15.321
not because
they're not as evolved as you are.

35:16.030 --> 35:17.698
They live on 'cause they need to.

35:20.118 --> 35:22.537
Geum-myeong, I'm sorry to ask this.

35:24.705 --> 35:26.582
Are you jealous of me or something?

35:27.583 --> 35:28.417
Me, why?

35:29.335 --> 35:33.089
Well, um, for several reasons.
I'm going abroad in place of you.

35:33.172 --> 35:36.008
You're only going
because I turned it down.

35:36.092 --> 35:37.927
Turned down? [laughs]

35:41.806 --> 35:42.974
Then maybe you should go.

35:44.517 --> 35:45.351
You can go.

35:55.778 --> 35:57.738
You're still acting
like as if you yielded it,

35:57.822 --> 36:01.117
but you don't get to go
just because your GPA is higher.

36:01.200 --> 36:03.119
Family circumstances
are all taken into account.

36:03.703 --> 36:06.372
Who said that? Was it your father?

36:07.748 --> 36:09.709
Events in life are decided
by multiple things.

36:16.507 --> 36:19.051
[young Ae-sun] I don't get it.
I got 37 votes.

36:19.135 --> 36:20.761
So what if you got 37 votes?

36:20.845 --> 36:22.555
So what if you got more votes?

36:22.638 --> 36:26.058
In the real world,
it doesn't even matter who got 37 votes.

36:26.142 --> 36:28.811
It's between Man-ki and you,
you understand?

36:28.895 --> 36:32.356
There's something that goes beyond
the nine-vote difference. All right, kid?

36:32.440 --> 36:33.482
CLASS MOTTO
HONESTY

36:34.692 --> 36:35.526
[teacher] Mm.

36:36.027 --> 36:36.861
Take it.

36:37.612 --> 36:39.113
Yeah, here. Take it.

36:40.281 --> 36:42.575
Leave it here. Take one. Hmm.

36:42.658 --> 36:46.412
Man-ki's dad brought buns to celebrate him
becoming class president, got it?

36:46.913 --> 36:48.789
You got snacks from him last time too.

36:48.873 --> 36:51.751
If you took food from Man-ki's family
but didn't vote for him,

36:51.834 --> 36:53.211
you'd better feel bad.

37:09.852 --> 37:13.356
If you're staying behind,
you'll only get a bun after you're done.

37:14.273 --> 37:16.275
[students moan]

37:18.402 --> 37:20.905
[teacher] Yeah, take one. Okay. Go ahead.

37:28.829 --> 37:30.081
DIARY
OH AE-SUN

37:41.968 --> 37:43.052
[chortles]

37:45.221 --> 37:46.305
[sighs]

37:49.892 --> 37:52.728
Man-ki, come on! Are you even studying?

37:52.812 --> 37:55.648
Are you sure you aren't just
eating cream buns at home?

37:55.731 --> 37:57.817
[young Ae-sun] Our class president
is a fake president,

37:57.900 --> 37:59.318
a cream bun president.

37:59.402 --> 38:03.364
Even if Man-ki had 100 cream buns,
he'd never score 100 points.

38:03.447 --> 38:05.032
I got 100 points.

38:05.116 --> 38:07.118
[lively music playing]

38:16.711 --> 38:18.629
[Geum-myeong] Mom was like a flower

38:18.713 --> 38:22.675
that found a way to grow
through the cracks into the sunlight.

38:22.758 --> 38:24.010
[worker] Let's hurry.

38:24.093 --> 38:26.345
[Geum-myeong]
She always found her light again.

38:29.390 --> 38:33.102
[middle-aged Ae-sun] I had my blind date
here with Bu Sang-gil many years ago.

38:33.769 --> 38:35.104
AUNTIES'
FRESHLY PICKED BY HAENYEO

38:35.187 --> 38:36.355
At the time,

38:36.939 --> 38:39.859
I really thought that
my life was already over.

38:44.697 --> 38:46.866
I heard you were after a man from Seoul.

38:48.284 --> 38:51.245
So, I'm practically from Seoul myself.

38:51.746 --> 38:54.707
I got an education on the mainland
as good as any in Seoul.

38:54.790 --> 38:57.126
Had I not moved here after I got married…

38:59.295 --> 39:01.297
[wistful music playing]

39:10.473 --> 39:12.433
[dishes clatter]

39:22.485 --> 39:25.321
-I mean, who says it's wrong to love?
-Goodness. [chuckles]

39:25.863 --> 39:28.282
Who would've thought I'd own this store?

39:29.325 --> 39:30.701
Like I say, in life,

39:30.785 --> 39:33.120
you never know what'll happen
unless you go for it.

39:33.204 --> 39:34.663
Go!

39:34.747 --> 39:37.875
And I even thought of
the name of the store.

39:37.958 --> 39:39.377
[laughter]

39:39.460 --> 39:42.963
Yeah, the educated one
better name the store.

39:43.798 --> 39:46.967
"Sun and the three Aunties."

39:47.760 --> 39:49.720
We don't need a name that's difficult.

39:49.804 --> 39:53.015
Even a poetry collection will sell well
if the title is understandable.

39:53.099 --> 39:55.726
Thousands of people are called
"Sun" in the world,

39:55.810 --> 39:58.729
so if we're able to attract them,
it'll be lots.

39:58.813 --> 40:00.356
You're so self-centered.

40:00.439 --> 40:01.774
-Let's do it!
-You are. Okay, okay.

40:01.857 --> 40:02.691
-Do it.
-Yes.

40:02.775 --> 40:03.984
-Yeah.
-Yeah, do it.

40:04.068 --> 40:07.530
Let's just stop having lunch
by the street from now on?

40:07.613 --> 40:08.823
I'm going

40:09.573 --> 40:10.950
to have lunch at a table.

40:11.450 --> 40:12.827
You eat at the table.

40:12.910 --> 40:14.870
So each of us gets a quarter?

40:14.954 --> 40:19.041
Ae-sun, you take what's left
and just pay for this section, okay?

40:19.125 --> 40:20.626
[Gyeong-ja] The water pressure is weak.

40:20.709 --> 40:22.878
-Huh?
-[woman 6] Oh, the water pressure.

40:22.962 --> 40:27.341
This is enough, right? You can manage
to clean sea cucumber and sea squirt.

40:28.092 --> 40:29.593
-I don't think so.
-I'll do the washing.

40:29.677 --> 40:32.304
[Geum-myeong] However,
while there was barely any water

40:32.388 --> 40:33.848
dripping out of the faucet,

40:36.767 --> 40:39.562
the money my family made
gushed out steadily.

40:41.147 --> 40:43.107
ELIGIBILITY FOR STATE-FUNDED STUDY ABROAD

40:43.190 --> 40:47.486
I just think it's odd
for an English lit major to go to Japan.

40:48.612 --> 40:50.656
It also means I'll graduate later,

40:51.240 --> 40:52.366
so I don't think…

40:54.034 --> 40:56.287
Well, I should…

41:04.587 --> 41:05.796
I, um,

41:06.797 --> 41:08.132
would like you to go.

41:09.425 --> 41:11.469
[sighs] Ye-rim is a little…

41:13.762 --> 41:14.597
uppity.

41:20.978 --> 41:24.273
Since you don't qualify
for the state-sponsored scholarship,

41:25.649 --> 41:26.817
as I said earlier…

41:26.901 --> 41:29.028
Oh, no, no, don't.

41:29.111 --> 41:30.112
Don't. Please don't.

41:30.196 --> 41:33.365
I'm going to leave, and I won't come back
if you call me again.

41:33.449 --> 41:36.285
No. My family has money.

41:37.661 --> 41:38.996
You can pay it back later.

41:40.456 --> 41:44.168
You told me your car was the cheapest
in the faculty lot before.

41:44.251 --> 41:47.546
What's so important about my situation?
You need to be brazen and take it now.

41:47.630 --> 41:49.256
Or you'll end up just like me.

41:49.340 --> 41:52.301
[chuckles] But you're
a fantastic person though.

41:52.801 --> 41:56.847
I'm pretty sure you're the only professor
who feeds apples to sparrows.

41:58.849 --> 42:02.102
But anyway, thank you so much
for looking out for me.

42:02.186 --> 42:03.604
From the bottom of my heart.

42:05.022 --> 42:06.774
Feels like I already went to Japan.

42:07.566 --> 42:09.276
You have a way with words, girl.

42:11.987 --> 42:15.491
[Geum-myeong] For others, it was as though
I was writing a love letter.

42:16.158 --> 42:19.620
I was mindful of every word
that came out of my mouth.

42:19.703 --> 42:23.123
Yeah, yeah,
she's such a good person. She is.

42:23.624 --> 42:25.709
[Geum-myeong] When others treat you well,

42:25.793 --> 42:27.920
you think
they're the greatest gift to you.

42:28.003 --> 42:29.046
PURCHASE AND SALE AGREEMENT

42:29.129 --> 42:32.550
[Geum-myeong] Yeah, so you have to send
the best tangerines you can find.

42:32.633 --> 42:34.093
She's so good to me.

42:34.176 --> 42:35.594
So what did she do for you?

42:35.678 --> 42:37.680
Say you did well, or she likes you?

42:38.180 --> 42:39.348
Oh, what did she say?

42:39.431 --> 42:41.559
I wanna hear
the nice things she said to you.

42:41.642 --> 42:45.688
Oh, she's about to take a loan out
to send me to study abroad.

42:45.771 --> 42:48.232
Not easy to do for someone else, right?

42:48.315 --> 42:51.527
She calls me to the faculty cafeteria
and buys me food.

42:52.027 --> 42:54.947
But you didn't want to study… abroad.

42:55.573 --> 42:56.907
That's what you said.

42:56.991 --> 43:00.035
I know. Just send me a box of tangerines.

43:00.536 --> 43:01.996
Do you wanna study abroad?

43:02.955 --> 43:03.998
You wanna go?

43:04.081 --> 43:09.086
Oh, but I couldn't go
even if I wanted to, right?

43:09.169 --> 43:10.212
Uh, how much is it?

43:11.046 --> 43:12.047
How much is it?

43:13.215 --> 43:14.550
You don't need to know.

43:14.633 --> 43:17.845
Well, I'm not saying I'll pay for it.
Just tell me how much it costs roughly.

43:17.928 --> 43:20.014
The Japanese yen costs so much.

43:20.097 --> 43:21.432
Don't you watch the news?

43:21.515 --> 43:24.018
Say how much it is.
Just tell me how much, at least.

43:24.101 --> 43:26.145
You're making me mad now.
You're not that needy.

43:26.228 --> 43:27.521
You have parents.

43:27.605 --> 43:30.065
Why should someone
have to take out a loan for you?

43:30.149 --> 43:31.900
What did you tell her for her to say that?

43:31.984 --> 43:34.153
You think I present like someone
who comes from wealth?

43:34.236 --> 43:37.531
All the kids at school know how poor
we are because I chose not to go to Japan.

43:37.615 --> 43:40.659
How much is it, then?
Tell me just how much it costs to go!

43:40.743 --> 43:43.746
So what if I tell you? You'll send me
to Japan with street vending money?

43:43.829 --> 43:45.706
If you can afford it,
stop selling on the street.

43:45.789 --> 43:48.167
Listen, I wanna stop too. I do.

43:48.250 --> 43:49.209
But how can I?

43:49.293 --> 43:50.502
[sighs]

43:54.340 --> 43:55.716
Whatever, forget it.

43:56.425 --> 43:57.801
Don't even send the box.

43:58.302 --> 44:00.220
Talking to you just makes me mad.

44:00.304 --> 44:01.513
[sighs]

44:01.597 --> 44:04.975
[Geum-myeong] But I treated the one I owed
my whole life to as harshly

44:05.059 --> 44:07.436
as if I was writing on scrap paper.

44:08.103 --> 44:09.355
[sighs]

44:10.648 --> 44:12.066
Oh, what now?

44:13.400 --> 44:15.152
[Geum-myeong] I wasn't mindful…

44:15.235 --> 44:18.364
-You always just drive me nuts.
-…of my words or my heart.

44:19.573 --> 44:21.575
[soft pop music playing]

44:27.456 --> 44:29.166
I don't qualify at all.

44:31.794 --> 44:32.753
[sighs]

44:38.133 --> 44:40.135
[thunder rumbling]

44:41.470 --> 44:42.596
[rain pattering]

45:23.595 --> 45:24.847
[Geum-myeong] How much is that?

45:24.930 --> 45:28.517
Just 300 won. Give me 300 won.

45:30.227 --> 45:32.229
[thunder rumbling]

45:32.938 --> 45:34.940
[soft pop music continues]

45:43.407 --> 45:45.451
How much for all of it, ma'am?

45:45.534 --> 45:46.368
Hmm?

45:47.119 --> 45:48.537
I like beans a lot.

45:49.580 --> 45:51.081
[Geum-myeong] A kind-hearted mother…

45:51.165 --> 45:53.459
[middle-aged Ae-sun]
…gave birth to a kind-hearted daughter.

45:53.542 --> 45:56.295
[Geum-myeong] They were loving
and fond of each other.

45:56.378 --> 45:58.505
[middle-aged Ae-sun]
And they broke each other's hearts.

45:59.131 --> 46:00.549
[music fades]

46:04.428 --> 46:06.305
Sure I wanna stop street vending.

46:06.930 --> 46:09.600
Who wants to be a street vendor
if they have a choice?

46:12.811 --> 46:14.438
Once I was coy and girly too.

46:14.938 --> 46:16.398
I was a bookworm as well.

46:17.149 --> 46:18.275
Jeez.

46:18.358 --> 46:19.651
You know when I see

46:19.735 --> 46:23.197
a friend from the past passing by
as I sit there eating on newspaper,

46:23.280 --> 46:25.407
I wanna stop eating the food right away.

46:26.366 --> 46:27.993
I lose my appetite for the whole day.

46:34.082 --> 46:36.794
[sighs] She's not the only one with pride.

46:36.877 --> 46:39.505
Does she think we live like this
because we lack pride?

46:40.881 --> 46:41.715
But what can we do?

46:41.799 --> 46:44.092
There are a lot of things
she wants to experience,

46:44.176 --> 46:47.054
and us not being able to provide them
makes me die inside.

46:51.850 --> 46:52.935
[sighs]

46:53.018 --> 46:55.229
I knew there was something wrong
when you started drinking

46:55.312 --> 46:57.523
each time you'd come home
from seeing Geum-myeong.

46:59.274 --> 47:03.904
Well… [tuts] …I have nothing to say anyway
to both you or her.

47:03.987 --> 47:04.905
So…

47:09.743 --> 47:11.203
My mom must've cried

47:12.913 --> 47:15.541
because back when
I didn't get to be class president,

47:16.250 --> 47:17.918
she couldn't provide for me.

47:18.794 --> 47:21.547
Oh, I get it now. I get it.

47:28.887 --> 47:30.180
What did she say?

47:30.806 --> 47:32.140
Did she cry about going abroad?

47:32.724 --> 47:33.892
Was she frustrated?

47:35.102 --> 47:36.728
[emotional music playing]

47:36.812 --> 47:39.565
[Geum-myeong] They sold their house
for their daughter,

47:41.233 --> 47:42.693
who will never grow up.

47:46.947 --> 47:49.449
These are our last persimmons. Look.

47:50.784 --> 47:52.244
You have them all, Ae-Sun.

47:52.327 --> 47:54.204
Don't give them to anybody else.

47:54.288 --> 47:56.331
[chuckles] Not even to the kids?

47:56.415 --> 47:59.334
Not even to the kids. Only for you.

47:59.418 --> 48:00.711
[laughs]

48:01.461 --> 48:04.506
We knew raising kids would only get
more and more expensive.

48:05.007 --> 48:07.092
We knew that about parenting
from the start.

48:07.175 --> 48:09.386
It's a losing business, isn't it?

48:11.805 --> 48:13.724
[Geum-myeong] She left the house behind.

48:14.933 --> 48:17.436
Her mother, her younger self,

48:19.646 --> 48:20.731
and Dong-myeong,

48:22.149 --> 48:23.859
whom she could never mention,

48:25.193 --> 48:26.236
would be missed.

48:33.702 --> 48:36.663
[distant clattering]

49:13.450 --> 49:14.409
[sighs]

49:19.748 --> 49:21.750
[tender piano music playing]

49:50.195 --> 49:53.281
Mom, I didn't… grasp how young you were.

49:54.491 --> 49:57.411
You need to get rid of the cracked ones.
Throw these out.

49:58.578 --> 50:02.541
I dreamed about you when we moved here.
Did you return 'cause we're leaving?

50:03.583 --> 50:05.293
It's bittersweet to see you.

50:05.794 --> 50:08.005
You should've visited me more
in my dreams.

50:09.631 --> 50:11.299
Oh, Mom, I'm so upset.

50:11.383 --> 50:14.928
I still have so many things
that I wanted to speak to you about.

50:16.513 --> 50:19.641
Why are you writing him a letter?
He can't even read.

50:21.018 --> 50:23.478
He never learned to read,
so what's the point?

50:24.730 --> 50:27.607
[middle-aged Ae-sun] In case
he comes to see us during the holidays.

50:27.691 --> 50:30.610
I didn't want him to be surprised
to see that we were gone.

50:32.779 --> 50:34.573
I didn't wanna scare the baby.

50:35.073 --> 50:37.284
[music fades]

50:41.830 --> 50:44.833
You and Gwan-sik…
still never talk about him?

50:48.045 --> 50:51.256
So why not talk… of Dong-myeong?

50:56.053 --> 50:57.095
Why would we?

50:58.805 --> 51:01.099
We already know
how we feel about his loss.

51:01.600 --> 51:04.352
With grief above anything else,
time can heal our sorrow

51:04.436 --> 51:05.562
and dull the pain.

51:06.396 --> 51:08.065
But when the grief is one that

51:08.648 --> 51:09.775
cuts so bad,

51:11.151 --> 51:12.277
you bury it.

51:13.528 --> 51:15.280
I… I can't bring it up with him.

51:20.410 --> 51:21.328
Ae-sun.

51:22.871 --> 51:24.206
Speak to him.

51:25.457 --> 51:26.291
Pour it out.

51:27.250 --> 51:28.418
The waves can reach

51:29.503 --> 51:30.796
the ocean floor

51:31.713 --> 51:33.965
and raise even the deepest waters.

51:37.803 --> 51:38.929
[chuckles]

51:40.722 --> 51:42.307
I'm sorry to say this to you.

51:43.600 --> 51:45.102
I know I shouldn't say it.

51:46.436 --> 51:48.438
I do love remembering you, but…

51:50.524 --> 51:51.608
but not Dong-myeong.

51:53.151 --> 51:54.402
Not my little boy.

52:05.747 --> 52:08.166
I just wanted for you to live a good life.

52:09.835 --> 52:12.129
I always wonder how you'll survive.

52:12.796 --> 52:14.965
How my baby will survive this.

52:15.465 --> 52:17.467
[emotional string music playing]

52:18.426 --> 52:22.514
I… do forget briefly
every once in a while.

52:24.099 --> 52:25.308
From time to time, yeah.

52:29.104 --> 52:31.898
Somehow, I'm surviving every day.

52:57.924 --> 53:00.427
THE MOON WANES,

53:00.510 --> 53:03.555
YET THE YOUNG HEART REMAINS.

53:03.638 --> 53:04.806
[Geum-myeong] Tomorrow.

53:05.390 --> 53:06.766
[mover 1] Hurry, this way.

53:09.060 --> 53:12.606
[Geum-myeong] Tomorrow,
we live under tomorrow's sun.

53:17.068 --> 53:20.614
[Eun-myeong] Oh, look, that plane.
Why are there so many of them, man?

53:31.249 --> 53:35.712
[indistinct announcement over PA]

53:40.884 --> 53:44.221
OPEN STUDY ABROAD POLICY
SPARKS SURGE IN STUDENTS GOING ABROAD

53:44.304 --> 53:45.597
[Geum-myeong sniffles]

53:47.432 --> 53:48.433
[sniffles]

53:51.186 --> 53:52.270
[sniffles]

53:53.480 --> 53:55.899
Why did she wrap this so tightly?

53:57.400 --> 53:59.402
Why did she do this?

54:01.154 --> 54:02.697
God. [sniffles]

54:15.835 --> 54:17.420
[breathes deeply]

54:23.134 --> 54:24.594
[sniffles]

54:28.139 --> 54:29.766
[sobs]

54:34.354 --> 54:36.690
Have a bit, crybaby.

54:41.653 --> 54:43.196
Thank you very much.

54:43.280 --> 54:44.239
Sure.

54:48.451 --> 54:49.452
[sniffles]

54:51.788 --> 54:52.789
[man] Are you okay?

54:59.004 --> 55:00.922
[wistful music playing]

55:01.006 --> 55:04.217
[Geum-myeong] I took their dreams
and spread my wings

55:05.260 --> 55:08.847
with the seeds of
my mom's dreams in my heart.

55:08.930 --> 55:10.932
[wistful music continues]

55:16.771 --> 55:19.065
[laughing]

55:25.155 --> 55:26.031
Is this funny?

55:26.990 --> 55:28.158
Is this funny to you?

55:29.617 --> 55:31.077
You know what? A bit.

55:33.246 --> 55:38.001
I wanted to go to college
so badly when I was younger.

55:38.084 --> 55:39.419
[laughs]

55:40.253 --> 55:42.839
But now, my daughter is off

55:42.922 --> 55:44.507
studying abroad.

55:45.592 --> 55:48.845
It just feels so good.
I'm proud of her, you know?

55:48.928 --> 55:50.263
So you're happy now?

55:52.057 --> 55:54.059
[groans] Jeez!

55:59.439 --> 56:00.523
[young Ae-sun] Mom!

56:01.316 --> 56:02.567
-Mom!
-[whistles]

56:02.650 --> 56:05.570
[middle-aged Ae-sun]
My mom passed her dreams on to me.

56:05.653 --> 56:07.655
[wistful music continues]

56:11.117 --> 56:14.913
[Geum-myeong]
My mom passed her dreams on to me.

56:21.127 --> 56:22.837
They were so heavy.

56:23.505 --> 56:25.423
They were scorching hot.

56:25.507 --> 56:26.341
[sobs]

56:26.424 --> 56:29.010
[middle-aged Ae-sun] When you kids soar,

56:30.011 --> 56:31.805
it's like I get to soar too.

56:32.347 --> 56:33.181
I do.

56:34.182 --> 56:37.268
[Geum-myeong]
Finally, their wings took flight.

56:38.603 --> 56:41.856
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

56:45.276 --> 56:46.194
DODONG GIRLS' HIGH

56:51.533 --> 56:54.244
Hey, did you get Ae-sun's consent?

56:54.953 --> 56:58.456
Why should writing contests be…
only for kids?

56:58.540 --> 57:01.793
The best cheeses are aged.
And to know something, you need to live.

57:02.293 --> 57:04.254
Kids don't comprehend life at all.

57:04.879 --> 57:06.673
[teacher on PA] One more time,

57:06.756 --> 57:09.092
will the student Oh Ae-sun

57:09.175 --> 57:12.262
please come immediately
to the faculty's office?

57:13.012 --> 57:14.013
Oh Ae-sun.

57:14.097 --> 57:17.684
I told you all
when students complete tests,

57:17.767 --> 57:21.229
there are some
who never specify their grade and class,

57:21.312 --> 57:23.314
even if you tell them over and over!

57:24.065 --> 57:27.652
Did I or did I not explain that
you need to tell them a hundred times?

57:29.654 --> 57:30.780
Did I or did I not?

57:32.699 --> 57:34.367
What, am I talking to a wall now?

57:34.868 --> 57:37.787
The winner is from our school,
and we can't find the student!

57:37.871 --> 57:39.956
What am I supposed to tell the principal?

57:42.292 --> 57:43.793
Goodness gracious!

57:43.877 --> 57:46.713
EVEN AS I GENTLY PRESS MY HEART
TO SOOTHE IT DOWN

57:46.796 --> 57:49.382
THE MOON WANES,
YET THE YOUNG HEART REMAINS.

57:49.466 --> 57:51.468
[upbeat funky music playing]

01:00:28.207 --> 01:00:29.375
[music ends]

01:00:34.839 --> 01:00:39.510
"IN THE HOPE THAT OUR ECHOES
WILL FLOW AND FLOW UNTIL THEY REACH YOU."
